1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:04,753
Creech Manor: over a hundred years old, full of historic charm, and every room has a

2
00:00:04,753 --> 00:00:05,655
horrifying story.

3
00:00:05,875 --> 00:00:07,624
Here's how the location plays.

4
00:00:08,433 --> 00:00:12,871
Creech Manor has no special setup, but the house itself has a few rules of its own.

5
00:00:13,700 --> 00:00:16,513
Three spaces only exit one way, shown by white arrows.

6
00:00:16,513 --> 00:00:20,420
You can't climb back up the tyre swing, or up through the washroom ceiling.

7
00:00:20,640 --> 00:00:24,905
Victims and Enemies follow the same rule, though the spaces still count as adjacent

8
00:00:24,905 --> 00:00:25,419
both ways.

9
00:00:25,639 --> 00:00:28,048
The Rope Ladder item is the only exception:

10
00:00:28,048 --> 00:00:30,737
it turns a one-way space back into a normal one.

11
00:00:31,567 --> 00:00:35,590
There are three Window spaces. They have no rules of their own, but lots of Terror

12
00:00:35,590 --> 00:00:36,964
and Event cards target them.

13
00:00:37,184 --> 00:00:41,211
The Ladder always means the outside ladder up to the third-floor washroom, never the

14
00:00:41,211 --> 00:00:41,835
attic ladder.

15
00:00:42,055 --> 00:00:45,639
And every space is Inside except the three exits, which are Outside.

16
00:00:46,467 --> 00:00:50,200
A few tips. The exits are at street level, so bring Victims down early.

17
00:00:50,420 --> 00:00:53,513
Avoid the Attic: Victims sent there tend to die in bulk.

18
00:00:53,733 --> 00:00:56,997
If Lights Out comes up, a Flashlight or Candle keeps you moving.

19
00:00:57,217 --> 00:01:01,392
It's one of the tougher locations, especially against the Poltergeist and the Birds.

20
00:01:01,392 --> 00:01:01,889
Good luck.

